   "notes": "The paper enumerates the full MM recipe with concentrations in Materials and Methods, so it is self-contained; element coverage in the target (Ca, Cl, Fe, glucose, K, Mg, Na, NH4, phosphate, SO4, Zn, O2) was already complete. This curation adds the concrete salt identities and molar concentrations (previously null). Phosphate buffer (34 mM NaH2PO4 + 64 mM K2HPO4, ~98 mM total) also serves as the buffer; no separate buffer, and no vitamins (MG1655 is prototrophic on glucose minimal medium). Base medium 63 (Tanaka 1967) contributes no hidden trace-metal/vitamin stock. 0.01 mM IPTG (inducer, not "
